  },
  "note": "Election of the whole Portstewart Urban District Council under the Elections and Franchise Act (Northern Ireland) 1946, polled Wednesday 16 October 1946 (not 18 September): Co. Londonderry's urban polls were taken that day (Belfast News-Letter, 15 October 1946, p. 5: 'Polling also takes place to-morrow in Coleraine, Portstewart, and Limavady'; 17 October, p. 5: polling at the Town Hall). Sixteen nominations for twelve seats were received by W. I. Cunningham, returning officer; eight of the nine members of the former council stood again (BNL 2 October 1946, p. 6). About 75 per cent of the electorate of 1,487 voted. Re-filed from 1946-09-18 to the poll date, 16 October 1946 (gap-fill 6 Nov 2026). Sitting members are those the Sentinel marks '(outgoing)'. The News-Letter prints 'R. Millar', the Sentinel 'R. Miller, J.P.' and the nominations 'Robert Miller, J.P.'.",
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 18 October 1946, p. 6 (council-audit, Nov 2026): R. Millar is recorded as Robert Millar (was Miller, as the nominations list of 2 October misprints him; the result prints Millar, as do his other Portstewart returns)."
